  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Optum Public Sector Solutions has $19.9B in federal contract obligations so far in FY2026. Optum received 30 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $664M, and obligations fell 11.5% year over year. Yearly obligations climbed from $8.9B in FY21 to $22.5B in FY25, then moved to $19.9B in FY26. The FY21 through FY26 series is $8.9B, $14.5B, $16.2B, $20.1B, $22.5B, and $19.9B respectively. The current-year totals are partial because they cover fiscal year to date. Readers should note that the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables report total contract values rather than current-year obligations. This snapshot shows scale, award frequency, and recent directional change for Optum Public Sector Solutions in the federal market. Use these figures to compare size and tempo against peers, budget cycles, and agency buying patterns.",
